<title>JAPAN: Copper surplus to grow to 577,000 T in 1998 - IWCC.</title>
<headline>Copper surplus to grow to 577,000 T in 1998 - IWCC.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global oversupply of refined copper will reach 214,000 tonnes in 1997 and grow to 577,000 tonnes in 1998, according to International Wrought Copper Council (IWCC) statistics.</p>
<p>The IWCC's copper statistics were compiled during its 53rd joint meeting with copper producing and marketing companies in Kobe, western Japan, last week, and given to Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The details of the IWCC's copper supply/demand forecasts are as follows (in thousands of tonnes):</p>
<p> - World mine output -	    1996	 1997	  1998</p>
<p> Total				10,762     11,306	11,980</p>
<p> Europe				  753	  741	   778</p>
<p> Africa				  657	  714	   734</p>
<p> Asia				    837	  835	   937</p>
<p> North America		     2,906	2,982	 3,049</p>
<p> South America		     3,551	3,851	 4,260</p>
<p> Australia/Oceania		   696	  771	   810</p>
<p> CIS, China and others	    1,362     1,412	 1,412</p>
<p> - World refined output -	 1996	 1997	  1998</p>
<p> Total				 12,349    13,145	13,896</p>
<p> Europe				 2,370     2,447	 2,479</p>
<p> Africa				   522	 543	   547</p>
<p> Asia				   1,937     2,036	 2,119</p>
<p> North America			3,139     3,275	 3,515</p>
<p> South America			2,287     2,711	 3,031</p>
<p> Australia/Oceania		    304	 298	   331</p>
<p> CIS, China and others	    1,790     1,835	 1,874</p>
<p> - World refined consumption -  1996	 1997	  1998</p>
<p> Total				 12,477    12,931	13,319</p>
<p> Europe				 3,577     3,650	 3,708</p>
<p> Africa				   118	 122	   124</p>
<p> Asia				   3,640     3,829	 3,979</p>
<p> North America			2,978     3,014	 3,070</p>
<p> South America			  426	 459	   486</p>
<p> Australia/Oceania		    170	 165	   165</p>
<p> CIS, China and others	    1,568     1,692	 1,787</p>
<p>Output/consumption balance  of refined copper		   -128	 214	   577</p>
<p>-- Eiichiro Tokumoto, Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
